From: Thomas Lukaszewicz <tluk@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:10:16 -0700
Subject: [Views] Prevent potential UAF in NativeWidgetAura::Show()

Both window_->Show() and Activate() notify aura::Window observers,
which are explicitly permitted to synchronously destroy window_ during
visibility notifications. Under NATIVE_WIDGET_OWNS_WIDGET or
CLIENT_OWNS_WIDGET ownership models, OnWindowDestroyed() deletes `this`.
Continuing execution in Show() after the window is destroyed results in
a heap-use-after-free when accessing member fields or invoking further
methods (e.g. Activate(), SetInitialFocus(), Minimize()).

Use a WeakPtr to verify that `this` and `window_` remain valid after
invoking window_->Show() and Activate(), returning early if destroyed.

Add a regression test covering synchronous widget destruction during
Show().

Fixed: 553140050
Change-Id: I855479577166b018d94388c3e5a0d6326c228390
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8423564
Reviewed-by: Allen Bauer <kylixrd@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Thomas Lukaszewicz <tluk@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1701883}

diff --git a/ui/views/widget/native_widget_aura.cc b/ui/views/widget/native_widget_aura.cc
index 33b87762cb4820708c2965b5c750ea9ff6e2d3d2..5338969c255def72292611169e31fd4a72eacfde 100644
--- a/ui/views/widget/native_widget_aura.cc
+++ b/ui/views/widget/native_widget_aura.cc
@@ -790,10 +790,24 @@ void NativeWidgetAura::Show(ui::mojom::WindowShowState show_state,
     disabler.emplace(window_);
   }
 
+  // `window_->Show()` and `Activate()` below fan out to aura::Window
+  // observers, which are explicitly permitted to synchronously destroy
+  // `window_` (see Window::NotifyWindowVisibilityChangedAtReceiver()). When
+  // that happens under NATIVE_WIDGET_OWNS_WIDGET or CLIENT_OWNS_WIDGET
+  // ownership, OnWindowDestroyed() deletes `this`, so the rest of this method
+  // must not run.
+  auto weak_this = weak_factory.GetWeakPtr();
+
   window_->Show();
+  if (!weak_this || !window_) {
+    return;
+  }
   if (delegate_->CanActivate()) {
     if (show_state != ui::mojom::WindowShowState::kInactive) {
       Activate();
+      if (!weak_this || !window_) {
+        return;
+      }
     }
     // SetInitialFocus() should be always be called, even for
     // SHOW_STATE_INACTIVE. If the window has to stay inactive, the method will
